@page "/showcase/fintech/ops/audit"
@layout FintechOpsLayout

<PageTitle>Audit log · Operations · @FintechSeedData.ProductName</PageTitle>

@* Operations see it: the console's guard keeps everyone else out, and the state shows the log to operations only. The shared
   log's column filters (Who, Action, Record) replace the page's former role and action filters; its history is kept. *@
<div class="container-fluid px-lg-4">
    <div class="tm-page-head">
        <div>
            <h1 class="tm-title">Audit log</h1>
            <p class="tm-lead">
                Who did what, and when, newest first: operations (approvals, holds, rejections, dispute decisions, AML triage and cases, customer notes, postings), the
                system (transfers held by the rules, AML alerts raised, scheduled postings, overdue disputes escalated), and customers (transfers, payees, cards, budgets, alerts, disputes,
                and sign-ins). Each record links to its page in the console. Account numbers only ever show their last four digits.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <Card Class="tm-card">
        <CardBody Class="p-3 p-lg-4">
            <p class="small text-body-secondary mb-3">
                <Icon Name="IconName.Lock" class="me-1" aria-hidden="true" />Kept for this browser tab. Entries can't be changed or deleted.
            </p>
            <ShowcaseAuditLog ExportFileName="banking-audit-log" />
        </CardBody>
    </Card>
</div>
